{"lines":[{"t":"But it was really a job best done by one person. The other teams tried to collaborate on","c":1,"y":0.10605780700133871,"h":0.017652761528994754,"x":0.084259310517057123,"w":0.69567804972330727},{"c":1,"t":"building the structure, and descended into confusion, with everyone getting in each other's","h":0.018235898551446694,"w":0.72035486857096354,"y":0.12096176807830605,"x":0.084267062573569543},{"y":0.13590145358173611,"w":0.74095779418945318,"x":0.082193040561384031,"h":0.019445300242645236,"c":1,"t":"way. Our team leader solved the challenge brilliantly. She simply asked everyone in the team"},{"y":0.1518593597661323,"w":0.70391738891601563,"t":"to move a piece a few centimetres, to comply with the rule, and then let the person in the","x":0.084250531254969591,"h":0.017017666667313636,"c":1},{"t":"team with an aptitude for puzzles like this build it alone. We finished before any other team.","y":0.16733197499474795,"w":0.72859598795572922,"x":0.082207157912149761,"h":0.017651528155143703,"c":1},{"y":0.18171246579866285,"h":0.019976648481209502,"c":1,"t":"My point is that the task wasn't really suited to teamworking, so why make it one?","w":0.64844512939453125,"x":0.082158070075758233},{"c":1,"w":0.71427347819010412,"t":"Teamwork can also lead to inconsistency - a common cause of poor sales. In the case of","x":0.082166787980547065,"h":0.019368559227394111,"y":0.20514021700664209},{"w":0.72447580973307302,"h":0.01722548229815124,"x":0.080162840752386721,"y":0.22176523295557315,"c":1,"t":"a smartphone that a certain company launched, one director wanted to target the business"},{"h":0.018270464471428327,"y":0.23613421173083537,"x":0.080161586462554807,"c":1,"t":"market, and another demanded it was aimed at consumers. The company wanted both","w":0.69777206420898441},{"c":1,"x":0.080124316457423017,"t":"directors to be involved, so gave the product a consumer-friendly name, but marketed it to.","y":0.25158814223232928,"w":0.72251698811848952,"h":0.018821762363537275},{"c":1,"t":"companies. The result was that it met the needs of neither group. It would have been better","x":0.080180444985826299,"w":0.72854649861653642,"h":0.016157286748448074,"y":0.26813149974016592},{"h":0.016142955236356338,"w":0.42819035847981762,"x":0.080149218823695356,"y":0.28332203757900065,"t":"to let one director or the other have his way, not both.","c":1},{"c":1,"y":0.30629043166112957,"h":0.018572137830395019,"w":0.72241516113281246,"t":"Now industriousness, or hard work. It's easy to mock people who say they work hard: after","x":0.080137692822156534},{"y":0.32180672065179361,"c":1,"x":0.080154374924338759,"t":"all, a hamster running around in a wheel is working hard - and getting nowhere. Of course","w":0.71829025268554691,"h":0.017984087531782933},{"h":0.017895217778685524,"w":0.71628041585286462,"t":"hard work is valuable, but only when properly targeted. Otherwise it wastes the resources","x":0.080138904097294988,"c":1,"y":0.33679831986400122},{"h":0.019487432652845138,"c":1,"x":0.078050219779601568,"t":"that companies value most - time and energy. And that's bad for the organisation.","y":0.35122251728359899,"w":0.65464528401692712},{"t":"There's a management model that groups people according to four criteria: clever, hard-","y":0.37500027291314786,"h":0.019217778712475986,"c":1,"w":0.70394531250000003,"x":0.078066664550968307},{"y":0.39030558148670758,"x":0.078134763534027818,"t":"working, stupid and lazy. Here 'lazy'means having a rational determination not to carry out","h":0.018241693049634189,"c":1,"w":0.72440541585286455},{"y":0.40586861297202992,"t":"unnecessary tasks. It doesn't mean trying to avoid work altogether. Most people display two","w":0.73067306518554687,"h":0.018894896490413871,"x":0.078090418405204601,"c":1},{"t":"of these characteristics, and the most valuable people are those who are both clever and","x":0.078189310914416027,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"y":0.42285041236328202,"w":0.70781890869140618},{"c":1,"h":0.019587079824351039,"w":0.73072769165039064,"x":0.075986150747692327,"t":"lazy: they possess intellectual clarity, and they don't rush into making decisions. They come","y":0.43641580940386282},{"y":0.45284527740069314,"w":0.71832560221354169,"h":0.018160133676337953,"c":1,"x":0.078094098190268829,"t":"up with solutions to save the time and energy spent by the stupid and hard-working group."},{"x":0.076056940643302373,"h":0.0174868407322466,"w":0.74293568929036458,"c":1,"y":0.46910494856738327,"t":"Instead of throwing more man-hours at a problem, the clever and lazy group looks for a more"},{"x":0.077932161699235447,"y":0.48346705514074384,"w":0.14458838144938149,"t":"effective solution.","c":1,"h":0.015215690621779299},{"c":1,"t":"Next we come to creativity. This often works well - creating an attention-grabbing TV","x":0.075993764317046172,"h":0.01992776059711221,"w":0.6751797993977865,"y":0.50504289332198038},{"y":0.52325581376984065,"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.078189294307986948,"t":"commercial, for example, might lead to increased sales. But it isn't always a good thing.","w":0.69753087361653643,"c":1},{"x":0.078079567179057494,"w":0.72035807291666665,"c":1,"t":"Some advertising campaigns are remembered for their creativity, without having any effect","y":0.53735711669436204,"h":0.018726497151405175},{"x":0.076075301733878012,"y":0.55347125152258259,"w":0.70793975830078126,"h":0.016417295548042499,"c":1,"t":"on sales. This happened a few years ago with the launch of a chocolate bar: subsequent"},{"h":0.015988312845937824,"c":1,"t":"research showed that plenty of consumers remembered the adverts, but had no idea what","x":0.076058920098567934,"y":0.56897882365808861,"w":0.72032018025716138},{"y":0.58442421272886569,"w":0.71830495198567712,"h":0.017612241603460421,"t":"was being advertised. The trouble is that the creator derives pleasure from coming up with","c":1,"x":0.076036822054484601},{"c":1,"h":0.018404056382825051,"x":0.075992736306078681,"t":"the idea, and wrongly assumes the audience for the campaign will share that feeling.","y":0.59941864535519185,"w":0.67722610473632816},{"t":"A company that brings out thousands of new products may seem more creative than a","x":0.076035150638849788,"y":0.62269613095248844,"h":0.017704554806047712,"w":0.68742482503255209,"c":1},{"x":0.076030772292542681,"w":0.73478205362955729,"h":0.018459181903529021,"c":1,"t":"company that only has a few, but it may be too creative, and make smaller profits. Creativity.","y":0.63824297846225209},{"h":0.021173223309017053,"w":0.74722930908203122,"c":1,"x":0.073925316209452863,"t":"needs to be targeted, to solve a problem that the company has identified. Just coming up with","y":0.65156505435865775},{"x":0.076131689203759928,"t":"more and more novel products isn't necessarily a good thing.","w":0.48765431722005215,"h":0.016024323880181046,"y":0.66860465138090486,"c":1},{"h":0.020175628302656179,"t":"And finally, excellence. We all know companies that claim they 'strive for excellence', but","x":0.073948296853512827,"y":0.69079341140016515,"w":0.7080645243326823,"c":1},{"y":0.70930232543440142,"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.07407407738342045,"t":"it takes a long time to achieve excellence. In business, being first with a product is more","w":0.69958847045898442,"c":1},{"t":"profitable than having the best product. A major study of company performance compared","c":1,"y":0.72360592076127095,"w":0.71414967854817712,"x":0.074002465813978416,"h":0.017268135353870173},{"y":0.73969375739126941,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"x":0.074074078162192816,"t":"pioneers - that is, companies bringing out the first version of a particular product - with","w":0.69341562906901044},{"c":1,"t":"tollowers, the companies that copied and improved on that product. The study found that the","w":0.73868311564127609,"h":0.014534883982160851,"x":0.072016466648123681,"y":0.75581395335335222},{"y":0.76992636147121751,"w":0.72853632609049479,"h":0.016669991159607545,"c":1,"x":0.07401184100790327,"t":"pioneers commanded an average market share of 29 percent, while the followers achieved."},{"h":0.017583707757776845,"w":0.69775451660156251,"t":"less than half that, only 13 percent - even though their product might have been better.","y":0.78478915551760953,"x":0.071911521938481063,"c":1},{"t":"Insisting on excellence in everything we do is time-consuming, wastes energy and leads","y":0.80791598881278348,"x":0.071891585631271362,"h":0.0186249229736688,"c":1,"w":0.70393356323242184},{"c":1,"y":0.82351491292589973,"t":"to losing out on opportunities. Sometimes, second-rate work is more worthwhile than","h":0.016626068223070334,"w":0.67707504272460928,"x":0.069903639018495015},{"c":1,"y":0.8366838511514989,"h":0.021649018052890767,"w":0.7328064982096355,"t":"excellence. 'Make sure it's excellent' sounds like a good approach to business, but the just-","x":0.071876465213978988},{"c":1,"t":"get-started' approach is likely to be more successful.","x":0.071916688496789047,"y":0.85420563889444157,"w":0.42407694498697918,"h":0.017373649475852515},{"x":0.39483721545198913,"t":"leltsresources.org","h":0.016453971009091628,"c":1,"y":0.96768258519867956,"w":0.2082209142049154},{"c":1,"h":0.013910782210818429,"x":0.86196891436804324,"y":0.063538794919133279,"t":"Test 5","w":0.062070401509602857},{"y":0.10901162774854367,"h":0.013081395583944611,"x":0.83744856027432657,"t":"Q34","c":1,"w":0.037037035624186254},{"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944611,"y":0.20930232539116722,"x":0.83539094718562068,"t":"Q35","w":0.037037035624186254},{"c":1,"h":0.013081394460653484,"w":0.037037035624186143,"y":0.34011627935034183,"t":"Q36","x":0.83333333367967655},{"y":0.39334808090641926,"x":0.83207455889802817,"t":"Q37","h":0.015740569825728468,"c":1,"w":0.039566691716512059},{"y":0.55668604632866714,"t":"Q38","x":0.8312757208298821,"w":0.037037035624186254,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"y":0.93604651143122397,"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"99","w":0.026748971939086874,"c":1,"x":0.88271604890699984}],"h":3395,"w":2400}